text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', "As The Rack enters the battlefield, choose an opponent.\\nAt the beginning of the chosen player's upkeep, The Rack deals X damage to that player, where X is 3 minus the number of cards in their hand.", 'At the beginning of each upkeep, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', "Banefire deals X damage to any target.\\nIf X is 5 or more, this spell can't be countered and the damage can't be prevented.", 'Blaze deals X damage to any target.', "Cast this spell only if you've cast another green spell this turn.\\nTrample", 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target noncreature spell.', 'Counter target spell.', "Counter target spell. Search its controller's graveyard, hand, and library for all cards with the same name as that spell and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", 'Create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token for each Elf you control.', 'Create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token for each Forest you control.', "Creature spells can't be countered.", 'Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control have double strike.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFirst strike", 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target non-Elf creature.', "Destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Draw X cards.', 'Each creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield that shares at least one creature type with it. (For example, if two Goblin Warriors and a Goblin Shaman are on the battlefield, each gets +2/+2.)', "Elven Riders can't be blocked except by Walls and/or creatures with flying.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each Forest you control.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nYou control enchanted creature.', 'Equipped creature gets +3/+0 and has trample and lifelink.\\nEquip {3}', 'Essence Drain deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nCrowd of Cinders's power and toughness are each equal to the number of black permanents you control.", 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nCloud Sprite can block only creatures with flying.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nOther black creatures get +1/+1.\\nNonblack creatures get -1/-1.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever Thieving Magpie deals damage to an opponent, draw a card.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Vampire this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Vampire.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Abyssal Specter deals damage to a player, that player discards a card.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', 'Green creatures you control have trample.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\n{T}: Kamahl, Pit Fighter deals 3 damage to any target.', "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\n{1}{G}: Regenerate Troll Ascetic.", "Hexproof\\nDrove of Elves's power and toughness are each equal to the number of green permanents you control.", 'If a source would deal damage to a permanent or player, it deals double that damage to that permanent or player instead.', "Incinerate deals 3 damage to any target. A creature dealt damage this way can't be regenerated this turn.", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\n{G}: Regenerate River Boa.", "Jagged-Scar Archers's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Elves you control.\\n{T}: Jagged-Scar Archers deals damage equal to its power to target creature with flying.", "Mortivore's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in all graveyards.\\n{B}: Regenerate Mortivore.", "Other Elf creatures get +1/+1 and have forestwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Other Elves you control get +1/+1.\\n{G}, {T}: Create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Red creatures you control have first strike.', "Return all creatures to their owners' hands.", "Return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Return target permanent card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Sacrifice Elvish Eulogist: You gain 1 life for each Elf card in your graveyard.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Spend only black mana on X.\\nConsume Spirit deals X damage to any target and you gain X life.', 'Tap all creatures without flying.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.', 'Target player discards X cards at random.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player gains 8 life.', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nMolimo, Maro-Sorcerer's power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.", "Trample\\nIf damage would be dealt to another creature you control, prevent that damage. Put a +1/+1 counter on that creature for each 1 damage prevented this way.\\nWhen Vigor is put into a graveyard from anywhere, shuffle it into its owner's library.", 'When Civic Wayfinder enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Denizen of the Deep enters the battlefield, return each other creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'When Elvish Visionary enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Ravenous Rats enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, Megrim deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, Underworld Dreams deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever you cast an Elf spell, you may create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', "{B}: Regenerate Drudge Skeletons. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{T}: Add {G}{G}.', '{T}: Cinder Pyromancer deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, you may untap Cinder Pyromancer.', '{T}: Prodigal Pyromancer deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature for each Elf you control.']
flavor: ['"A flash of the lightning, a break of the wave,\\nHe passes from life to his rest in the grave."\\n—William Knox, "Mortality"', '"A stick is your friend. A pointed stick is your good friend. An army of pointed sticks is your best friend."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"Before armor, there was bark. Before blades, there were thorns."\\n—Molimo, maro-sorcerer', '"Born under the moon, the second child will stumble on temptation and seek power in the dark places of the heart."\\n—Codex of the Constellari', '"For what are leaves but countless blades\\nTo fight a countless foe on high."\\n—Elvish hymn', '"From the sea came all life, and to the sea it will return. The sooner the better."\\n—Emperor Aboshan', '"Gaea sings with the voice of nature rampant: a thousand howls, chitters, and cries, and none of them can be ignored."', '"If the whole world burns, I\'ll never grow cold."', '"In the drowsy dark cave of the mind, dreams build their nest with fragments dropped from day\'s caravan."\\n—Rabindranath Tagore', '"It\'s a vicious circle. Stress breeds pain. Pain breeds stress. It\'s simply beautiful, wouldn\'t you agree?"\\n—Vradeen, vampire nocturnus', '"Jewels cannot be eaten nor gold drunk. What civilization trades, nature simply provides."\\n—Molimo, maro-sorcerer', '"No matter how adept our artistic skill, our effigies can never hope to capture the vibrant beauty of a living elf. Perhaps that is truly why we mourn."', '"Once I saw a goblin shouting at a thunderstorm. He lost the argument pretty quickly."\\n—Wandering mage', '"Once I supply the breeze, you\'ll see your warriors for the smoke they truly are."\\n—Alexi, zephyr mage', '"Rage courses in every heart, yearning to betray its rational prison."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The East Wind, an interloper in the dominions of Westerly Weather, is an impassive-faced tyrant with a sharp poniard held behind his back for a treacherous stab."\\n—Joseph Conrad, *The Mirror of the Sea*', '"The beauty of mental attacks is that your victims never remember them."\\n—Volrath', '"The construction of a defense is not accomplished by adding bricks."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"The dead make good soldiers. They can\'t disobey orders, never surrender, and don\'t stop fighting when a random body part falls off."\\n—Nevinyrral, *Necromancer\'s Handbook*', '"The elves are right: Death inevitably leads to life. But the truly powerful don\'t just experience this cycle. They control it."\\n—Crovax, ascendant evincar', '"The light of beauty protects our journeys through darkness."', '"These alleys are not safe. Come, I can guide you back to the market square."', '"Those without beauty are Lorwyn\'s greatest tumor. The winnowers have an unpleasant duty, but a necessary one."\\n—Eidren, perfect of Lys Alana', '"What am I looking at? Ashes, dead man."', '"Why fight the body when you can dominate the mind that rules it?"\\n—Jace Beleren', '"Wirewood cannot hide great size. Only with speed and skill can we survive here."', '"Yes, I think \'toast\' is an appropriate description."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', 'A banner for bonds of blood or belief.', 'A wurm knows nothing of deception. If it opens its mouth, it plans to eat you.', 'According to merfolk legend, a denizen of the deep swallows the horizon at the end of each day, bringing on the cold blanket of night.', 'Armodons are trained to step on things. Enemy things.', 'As graceful as a deer leaping a stream and as deadly as the wolf waiting in ambush on the other side, elvish warriors are the eyes of the forest as well as its unsheathed claws.', "Bears aren't always as strong and as mean as you imagine. Some are even stronger and meaner.", 'Before any major undertaking, a Cylian elf seeks the guidance of a visionary to learn the will of the gargantuan ancients.', 'Boggarts divide the world into two categories: things you can eat, and things you have to chase down and pummel before you can eat.', 'Bright as a mirror, dark as the sea.', 'Dark thoughts hatch and twist within the mind, straining to take wing.', 'Early Jamuraan hunters devised a weapon that would return to its source. Tolarian Æthermancers developed a spell that skipped the weapon entirely.', 'Earth elementals have the eternal strength of stone and the endurance of mountains. Primordially connected to the land they inhabit, they take a long-term view of things, scorning the impetuous haste of short-lived mortal creatures.', 'Elves of the immaculate class weave flora into living creatures—sometimes to endorse an elite warrior, sometimes to create a breathing work of art.', 'Empires rise and fall, but evil is eternal.', 'Fire never dies alone.', "For Sarkhan Vol, the dragon is the purest expression of life's savage splendor.", 'Fortunately, hill giants have large blind spots in which a human can easily hide. Unfortunately, these blind spots are beneath the bottoms of their feet.', "Foul-tempered, poorly trained, and mule-stubborn, the drake is the perfect test of the master's will.", 'Fragments of thought refract and multiply, surging in a geyser of dizzying insight.', "From the highest tiers of Dawn's Light Palace to the deepest shade of Wren's Run, the silver notes of the horn shimmer through the air, and all who hear it feel its pull.", "His soul snared by an angel's curse, Crovax twisted heroism into its purest shadow.", 'If you want to destroy something lifeless, make it live.', 'Imps are just intelligent enough to have an understanding of cruelty.', 'In a culture of beauty, the most beautiful are worshipped as gods.', 'In times when freedom seems lost, great souls arise to reclaim it.', 'Its curve mimics the twists of life and death.', 'Its spines act like the teeth of a saw, scoring distinctive marks in the vegetation of its territory.', 'Left to itself, nature overflows any container, overthrows any restriction, and overreaches any boundary.', 'Like nature, the fern spirals back on itself, eternally seeking its own center.', "Mages routinely summon creatures from the Æther. It's only fair that they occasionally throw one back.", 'Masters of the arcane savor a delicious irony. Their study of deep and complex arcana leads to such a simple end: the ability to say merely yes or no.', 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', 'No one in Aphetto answers a knock at the door after sundown.', 'Nothing is sacred to rats. Everything is simply another meal.', 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', "Once he'd worked out which end of the thing was sharp, he was promoted to guard duty.", 'Orcish lumberjacks spent the night sharpening their blades and resting for a day of labor. They awoke to find that the forest had been making its own preparations.', 'Other birds collect twigs for their nests. Magpies collect jewels for theirs.', 'Some wizards compete not to summon the most interesting creatures, but to create the most interesting aftereffects when a summons goes awry.', 'The barbarians call it "touching the soul of the dragon."', "The delicate sprites carry messages for Saprazzans, but they refuse to land in Mercadia City's filthy markets.", 'The faultless and immaculate castes form the lower tiers of elvish society, with the exquisite caste above them. At the pinnacle is the perfect, a consummate blend of aristocrat and predator.', 'The furnace awaits the next master who would stoke the fires of apocalypse.', "The giant spider's silk naturally resists gravity, almost weaving itself as it blankets the forest canopy.", 'The goblin word for "flying" is more accurately translated as "falling slowly."', "The murderous horrors of Raven's Run are legendary, but even that haunted place goes quiet when the night wolves howl.", 'The other tribes call them fanatics, but none deny that the Mul Daya elves have an iron-strong bond to some force greater than themselves.', 'The undisputed master of the mountains of Shiv.', 'They envy the life-giving heat so much that they tear it from those who still possess it.', 'Though no longer attached to the hand, it still holds its adversary in its grasp.', 'To gaze under its hood is to invite death.', 'Vengeance is a dish best served twice.', 'Winnowers live to eliminate eyeblights, creatures the elves deem too ugly to exist.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Ben Thompson', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Carl Frank', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'David Palumbo', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Gary Leach', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Staples', 'Izzy', 'Jeffrey R. Busch', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'John Matson', 'Jon Foster', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Larry MacDougall', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Nic Klein', 'Nick Percival', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paolo Parente', 'Paul Bonner', 'Pete Venters', 'Puddnhead', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spears', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sam Wood', 'Scott Bailey', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Ellis', 'Steve Luke', 'Steven Belledin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Terese Nielsen & Ron Spencer', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Una Fricker', 'Wayne England', "William O'Connor", 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai']
